Build-time / linked dependencies (not vendored)
-----------------------------------------------

* ESP-IDF (Espressif IoT Development Framework) — Apache-2.0
  Usage    : SDK and toolchain for the firmware/ applications and the
             components/routeloom_espnow adapter (which REQUIRES the IDF
             builtin components esp_wifi, esp_event, esp_netif,
             esp_timer, freertos, nvs_flash and mbedtls — mbedTLS,
             Apache-2.0, provides the PSA AES-GCM backend). Pinned to
             tag v6.0.3 (commit 76f5dedd9950a3012fee8fb7d5586df21fc67802,
             asserted in CI). Fetched via the espressif/idf container
             image or a normal ESP-IDF install; no ESP-IDF source is
             vendored here.
  Upstream : https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf

Rust crates (host workspace; exact versions pinned in host/Cargo.lock)
---------------------------------------------------------------------

Direct dependencies:

* rusqlite — MIT (https://github.com/rusqlite/rusqlite)
  Used with the "bundled" feature, which compiles the SQLite
  amalgamation (public domain, https://sqlite.org) into the binary via
  libsqlite3-sys (MIT). No system SQLite is required.
* crossterm — MIT (https://github.com/crossterm-rs/crossterm)

Transitive dependencies resolve to MIT, Apache-2.0, MIT OR Apache-2.0,
Zlib, or "Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT" licensed
crates (e.g. bitflags, cc, cfg-if, errno, fallible-iterator,
fallible-streaming-iterator, foldhash, hashbrown, hashlink, libc,
libsqlite3-sys, linux-raw-sys, lock_api, log, mio, parking_lot,
parking_lot_core, pkg-config, rustix, scopeguard, shlex, signal-hook,
signal-hook-mio, signal-hook-registry, smallvec, plus Windows-only
support crates). The authoritative list of resolved versions is
host/Cargo.lock; each release also publishes a generated SBOM
(CycloneDX JSON) enumerating every resolved crate and its license.

